  "result": "Fixed in `src/click/shell_completion.py`. I checked it with a quick one-off call to `split_arg_string`, and I did not run the test suite or add a test.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` uses `shlex`, which treats `#` as the start of a comment by default. Everything from the `#` onward was dropped from `COMP_WORDS`, so completion saw a truncated command line.\n\n**Fix:** I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is an ordinary character. `split_arg_string(\"prog a#b #c\")` now returns `['prog', 'a#b', '#c']`.\n\nI didn't add a changelog entry or a regression test. Say if you want either.",
